{
    "background_story": "Cal was a linguist with a passion for preserving Norway's cultural heritage. Growing up in a family of Nynorsk speakers, he was fascinated by the unique grammar and vocabulary of this lesser-known Norwegian dialect. As a young researcher, Cal dedicated himself to studying and promoting Nynorsk, often traveling to rural communities to document its usage. His work took him to the fjords of western Norway, where he met with elderly speakers who shared their stories and traditions. Cal's research helped to raise awareness about the importance of Nynorsk in Norwegian identity, and he became a leading advocate for its inclusion in educational curricula. Through his tireless efforts, Cal ensured that this vital part of Norway's linguistic heritage would continue to thrive for generations to come.",
